"I am writing to apply for the Forward Deployed AI Scientist position at BCG X in the United Kingdom. I am currently completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, after graduating from Imperial College London, with A-level Mathematics at A*, Chemistry at A* and Biology at A. Across my academic and professional experience I have framed ambiguous business problems, built and deployed machine learning and LLM systems, and presented the results directly to the clients who had to act on them. I am particularly interested in this role because it combines advanced analytics, software delivery and client-facing consulting rather than separating them.",

"What attracts me most to BCG X is owning the full analytics value chain, from framing a new business challenge through to deploying something the client can actually run. The work I am proudest of has followed exactly that arc. I enjoy taking an unclear business or clinical problem, working out what the underlying question really is, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested, measured and improved. The opportunity to do that across industries, with a team of 3,000 technical specialists behind it, strongly matches the kind of work I want to pursue.",

"In my most recent client engagement, at DS Digital Technology, a pharmaceutical client needed to know whether an AI system could be trusted to answer patients' questions about bone metastasis, and had no way to measure it. I framed the problem, designed a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension safety rubric with red-line rules, then built a Python pipeline connecting six large language models with retrieval augmentation, with concurrency, retries, structured validation and checkpointing so it could run reliably at scale. It produced and scored more than 2,400 responses through an LLM-as-judge framework, with human review on a sample to validate the judge itself. The client adopted the rubric as their acceptance standard. On a separate engagement I ran a repeated-measures analysis across 12 Apple and Tmall audience segments and 15 advertising touchpoints, using Friedman tests, randomised complete block ANOVA and permutation methods, and delivered per-segment media playbooks.",

"On the mathematical side, my MSc dissertation estimates individual-level counterfactual cardiovascular risk across 458,840 UK Biobank participants using doubly robust causal forests, with overlap weighting, E-values and quantitative bias analysis to test the assumptions that make those estimates credible. Modern machine learning is only as useful as your ability to say when it should not be believed, and most of that project was spent on exactly that question. I deployed the result as a Streamlit application so non-technical users could explore it.",

"On building things, I designed and shipped Jobwinner, a seven-agent due-diligence platform: a disambiguation agent, five domain specialists running in parallel on filtered evidence to control hallucination, and two synthesizers that reweight the same findings for investor and candidate audiences. It runs on Gemini 2.5 Flash and Pro, Tavily and GitHub APIs, a FastAPI backend and ClickHouse, with every finding cited. I work in Git and Docker daily and use Claude Code for code review, treating its output as a draft to check rather than an answer.",

"My earlier consulting experience at Ipsos Strategy3 and IQVIA prepared me for client-facing delivery. I analysed healthcare and consumer datasets and more than 80 expert interviews, built market-sizing and forecasting models estimating \\$20M of revenue potential, and translated the findings into executive dashboards and recommendations. I currently work as a data analyst at TikTok Shop UK, presenting analysis to operations, product and commercial stakeholders under commercial deadlines.",

"I would bring BCG X strong Python, a genuine grasp of the mathematics behind modern machine learning, experience shipping working systems rather than notebooks, and the ability to explain both to a non-technical client. I should be straightforward about seniority: I am early in my career, and my delivery experience comes from internships and client engagements rather than years of them. If the role is pitched above that, I understand. If BCG X is open to someone with the technical depth and client instinct but a shorter track record, I would very much like to be considered.",

"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience fits the Forward Deployed AI Scientist role and BCG X's work deploying AI solutions with clients.",
